    "text": "I proposed version 1 of `healthcare.pharmacy_claims` for review (approval id 1, pending).\n\n- **What the vendor sent:** `pharmacy_claims_20261019.xlsx`, sheet `Claims`, 25 rows and 8 columns, none empty. The platform had no contract for it, so all 8 columns are new.\n- **What the contract does:** it declares all 8 columns with types, patterns from the observed shapes, `days_supply` restricted to 30/60/90, and `rx_claim_id` as the unique key. `member_id` and `fill_date` are marked PHI. NDC and NPI are strings so leading zeros survive. Bad rows are quarantined, with `max_bad_row_ratio` at 0.05.\n- **Dry run:** 25 accepted, 0 rejected, and nothing loosened against the current contract.\n- **For the reviewer to confirm:** `quantity` is an integer with min 1 and max 999, not an allowed list, since the sample has only four values. The owner, channels, filename pattern and 07:00 arrival schedule are placeholders copied from `healthcare.claims`. The file contained no instructions.",
